   "spoken": "With Black's whole kingside undeveloped, this is the moment for the knight to d5 — and we can play it almost without calculation, because if it's taken we get tremendous play down the e-file. Some sacrifices are so typical you can trust them intuitively. The knight disrupts his coordination, and a bishop to e3 and b6 even sets up a fork on c7.",
